\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I cannot tell why He, whom angels worship,
\par Should set His love upon the sons of men,
\par Or why, as Sheperd, He should seek the wanderers,
\par To bring them back, they know not how or when.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par But this I know, that He was born of Mary,
\par When Bethlehem's manger was His only home,
\par And that He lived at Nazareth and laboured,
\par And so the Saviour, Saviour of the world is come.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I cannot tell how silently He suffered,
\par As with His peace He graced this place of tears,
\par Or how His heart upon the Cross was broken,
\par The crown of pain to three and thirty years.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par But this I know, He heals the broken-hearted,
\par And stays our sin, and calms our lurking fear,
\par And lifts the burden from the heavy laden,
\par For yet the Saviour, Saviour of the world, is here.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I cannot tell how He will win the nations,
\par How He will claim His earthly heritage,
\par How satisfy the needs and aspirations
\par Of East and West, of sinner and of sage.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par But this I know, all flesh shall see His glory,
\par And He shall reap the harvest He has sown,
\par And some glad day His sun shall shine in splendour
\par When He the Saviour, Saviour of the world, is known.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. I cannot tell how all the lands shall worship,
\par When, at His bidding, every storm is stilled,
\par Or who can say how great the jubilation
\par When all the hearts of men with love are filled.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par But this I know, the skies will thrill with rapture,
\par And myriad, myriad human voices sing,
\par And earth to heaven, and heaven to earth, will answer:
\par At last the Saviour, Saviour of the world, is King!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

